Prefer the video-only WFD profile over the AAC variants.

GND's pulsesrc reads its own null-sink monitor, and here it dies mid-session:

  audiosrc <pulseaudio-source-gnome-network-displays> error reading data -1
           (reason: Success), skipping segment
  rtspmedia gst_rtsp_media_set_state: media 0x... was not prepared   (+47ms)

The audio branch takes the RTSP media down with it, so nothing streams at all.
mpegtsmux is an aggregator and will not produce output while one of its sink
pads is broken.

Every video encoder in the table already has an ELEMENT_AUDIO_NONE variant; it
was just ranked below the three AAC ones, and GND picks the first profile whose
elements are all present. This promotes it. Casting is video-only as a result,
which is close to free here: GND's audio path requires manually routing
applications into the "Network-Displays" sink to carry anything anyway.

Not upstreamed.

